{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb2pt3b1ms","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gate labeler policy: inject plus note used but task failed is labeled FP not TP","summary":"Labeling-policy decision (2026-06-12) made while building scripts/gate-label.js. The four-quadrant design ([[note-mqasdxx0tnt]]) specified inject+note-used+pass=TP and inject+not-referenced=FP, but left the inject+note-used+FAIL cell unstated. Resolved: label it FP (label=0). Rationale: the training target is 'did injecting the note HELP?' — if the task failed even though the agent read the note, the injection did not help, so it is a negative example regardless of the note being referenced. The note-used signal alone does not earn a positive label; the OUTCOME must also be good. Consistent with outcome-grounded labeling. Consuming training stage must treat note_used as necessary-but-not-sufficient for a positive label. Discovered during task 6c89a72a/2.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T15:20:42.119Z","vec":[-0.030123235657811165,0.022792784497141838,-0.023382458835840225,-0.03455283120274544,0.018567394465208054,0.03378843888640404,0.054789844900369644,0.04046234115958214,-0.02456013485789299,-0.0003791161288972944,0.05093369260430336,-0.05891615152359009,-0.02184124104678631,0.05908968299627304,0.06550491601228714,0.04495106637477875,0.06931300461292267,-0.1504502296447754,0.04470448940992355,-0.11271999776363373,-0.01592886447906494,0.0389583446085453,0.04408137500286102,0.09549812227487564,-0.09398838132619858,0.007729565259069204,-0.10939597338438034,0.011189574375748634,0.029706666246056557,0.0437895692884922,-0.061854615807533264,0.07892095297574997,-0.051494646817445755,-0.043346572667360306,0.06653694063425064,0.11364094913005829,-0.07019922137260437,-0.009282139129936695,0.06307721883058548,-0.07768862694501877,0.03497928008437157,-0.04138946533203125,-0.031259141862392426,0.0027046911418437958,0.016071395948529243,0.015501298010349274,0.034001823514699936,-0